# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. `modules/` is **source content that gets emitted into
# other repositories**, and several engines match it with `^…$` multiline
# regexes. On a checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on GitHub's
# Windows runners, and on many Windows installs — every one of those lines gains
# a `\r`, the anchors stop matching, and a gate reports a rule as missing when it
# is present.
#
# Found by the CI matrix on its first run: `the shipped work-item skill carries
# the extension its module opted into` failed on windows-latest and passed on
# this machine, whose `core.autocrlf` happens to be `false`. The difference was
# never in the code (F-034).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets keep their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
